ooked older, yet somehow impossibly young. Her dark hair, once worn in loose waves, was now pulled back tightly, revealing the sharp line of her cheekbones. She wore a coat that was too thick for the season, and her eyes\u2014wide, dark, and filled with a fear that mirrored his own\u2014searched his face.\n\n\"Eli?\" she breathed, the name falling between them like a secret.\n\nHe wanted to run to her. He wanted to ask how she had found him, how she had come back after the years they had lost to silence and distance. But the words stuck in his throat. There was too much unsaid, too much time that had passed without a single word exchanged.\n\nInstead, he just stood there, the door half-open, the two of them suspended in the liminal space between the past and the present, waiting to see if either of them would break the spell first.", "annotations": []}]}], "usage": {"total_tokens": 491, "input_tokens": 87, "input_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}, "output_tokens": 404, "output_tokens_details": {"reasoning_tokens": 0}}}, "ts": "2026-11-25T05:15:39.774981+00:00"}
